01:24:16,753 --> 01:24:19,322
Well...

2289
01:24:19,355 --> 01:24:21,090
Well, it's not like
I'm tasting my own sweat

2290
01:24:21,123 --> 01:24:23,358
in this suit--
would you hurry up?

2291
01:24:25,262 --> 01:24:26,628
[Whispering]
For sure.

2292
01:24:26,662 --> 01:24:27,697
Well, would you look?

2293
01:24:27,730 --> 01:24:30,100
All the canned peaches
you could want!

2294
01:24:30,133 --> 01:24:32,968
... radiation is
a decontamination spray,

2295
01:24:33,002 --> 01:24:35,172
which reduces the level
of radiation...

2296
01:24:35,205 --> 01:24:39,808
Benedictus qui venit
in nomine domini.

2297
01:24:39,842 --> 01:24:43,212
Amen.

2298
01:24:43,245 --> 01:24:45,815
... that were all that man could
use against forces

2299
01:24:45,848 --> 01:24:48,250
too large for him to comprehend.

2300
01:24:48,283 --> 01:24:49,585
Tune in tomorrow.

2301
01:24:49,618 --> 01:24:52,388
In the director's cut,
they eliminated the narration.

2302
01:24:52,422 --> 01:24:53,590
- Oh.
- Hmm.

2303
01:24:53,623 --> 01:24:54,857
♪♪

2304
01:24:54,890 --> 01:24:56,458
♪ eee-oh ♪

2305
01:24:56,492 --> 01:24:59,095
Come on, dummy.

2306
01:24:59,128 --> 01:25:01,663
If we don't find grandma,
can we come up?

2307
01:25:03,165 --> 01:25:05,435
Uh, you think I should
tell him his zipper's down?

2308
01:25:05,468 --> 01:25:07,637
Ah.

2309
01:25:07,670 --> 01:25:08,938
[Pinging]

2310
01:25:08,972 --> 01:25:10,307
♪ Nightmare the clown ♪

2311
01:25:10,340 --> 01:25:12,342
♪ he's coming to your town,
hey ♪

2312
01:25:12,375 --> 01:25:15,312
[Goofy laughter
and grunting]

2313
01:25:15,345 --> 01:25:16,913
Ooh.

2314
01:25:27,490 --> 01:25:29,758
Time for your medication,
Mr. Taylor.

2315
01:25:29,792 --> 01:25:32,728
No, she's not one
of the Germans, Mr. Taylor.

2316
01:25:32,762 --> 01:25:35,298
[Pinging]

2317
01:25:39,435 --> 01:25:41,770
So I said to the kid, "either
get a job or get a haircut."

2318
01:25:41,803 --> 01:25:43,540
No kid's gonna live in my house
like that.

2319
01:25:43,573 --> 01:25:45,375
- Nah, I know what you mean.
- Ahh.

2320
01:25:45,408 --> 01:25:47,110
What are you gonna do?

2321
01:25:47,143 --> 01:25:48,343
So, lunch?

2322
01:25:48,377 --> 01:25:50,480
- Ah, okay.
- Yeah.

2323
01:25:50,513 --> 01:25:52,048
[Pinging continues]

2324
01:25:52,082 --> 01:25:55,285
It's "American gothic"
on a rampage.

2325
01:25:55,318 --> 01:25:57,953
He's not bad,
he's just misunderstood.

2326
01:26:00,290 --> 01:26:02,025
So what do you want to do
when we're done?

2327
01:26:02,058 --> 01:26:04,093
Oh, let's go to ginos.

2328
01:26:04,127 --> 01:26:06,062
Hey, how hot
is your suit, Bob?

2329
01:26:06,095 --> 01:26:07,230
I'm sweating bbs.

2330
01:26:07,263 --> 01:26:08,497
- Mm.
- Mm.

2331
01:26:08,532 --> 01:26:10,500
As if a switch
had been turned,

2332
01:26:10,533 --> 01:26:13,202
as if an eye had
been blinked,

2333
01:26:13,235 --> 01:26:15,472
as if some phantom force
in the universe

2334
01:26:15,505 --> 01:26:18,708
had made a move
eons beyond our comprehension...

2335
01:26:18,742 --> 01:26:19,975
As if we cared.

2336
01:26:20,008 --> 01:26:22,012
... suddenly,
there was no trail.

2337
01:26:22,045 --> 01:26:24,713
There was no giant,
no monster,

2338
01:26:24,747 --> 01:26:28,250
no thing
called Douglas to be followed.

2339
01:26:28,283 --> 01:26:29,518
There was nothing
in the tunnel

2340
01:26:29,552 --> 01:26:31,420
but the puzzled
men of courage

2341
01:26:31,453 --> 01:26:35,725
who suddenly found themselves
alone with shadows and darkness.

2342
01:26:35,758 --> 01:26:39,428
There was no dignity for anyone
who worked on this film!

2343
01:26:39,462 --> 01:26:41,397
Huh, well,
this was a bust.

2344
01:26:41,430 --> 01:26:42,832
Let's get out of here.

2345
01:26:45,067 --> 01:26:48,037
Come on, let's call the movie
on account of darkness.

2346
01:26:48,070 --> 01:26:49,438
That's a wrap, everyone!

2347
01:26:49,472 --> 01:26:51,807
Strike the set.

2348
01:26:51,840 --> 01:26:54,410
Turned out to be an alien
snipe hunt, go figure.

2349
01:26:54,443 --> 01:26:55,512
This was a test.

2350
01:26:55,545 --> 01:26:56,812
Had this been
an actual movie,

2351
01:26:56,845 --> 01:27:00,082
you would have been
entertained.

2352
01:27:00,115 --> 01:27:03,285
Phil silvers
tries to flee the set.

2353
01:27:03,318 --> 01:27:05,655
Um, uh, this is a note
from the director.

2354
01:27:05,688 --> 01:27:07,457
"Thank you, everybody,
the film is over."

2355
01:27:07,490 --> 01:27:09,325
Not everybody
will get paid tonight.

2356
01:27:09,358 --> 01:27:10,827
You'll have
to check the sheet, okay?

2357
01:27:10,860 --> 01:27:12,695
What the...

2358
01:27:12,728 --> 01:27:15,163
It says, "sell the house,
sell the car, sell the kids.

2359
01:27:15,197 --> 01:27:17,267
I'm never coming back"?

2360
01:27:17,300 --> 01:27:18,567
... and another descends.

2361
01:27:18,602 --> 01:27:21,803
Astronaut frank Douglas
rescued,

2362
01:27:21,837 --> 01:27:24,973
alive, well,
and of normal size

2363
01:27:25,007 --> 01:27:27,443
some 8,000 miles away
in a lifeboat.

2364
01:27:27,477 --> 01:27:29,278
- Oh, come on!
- Wait a minute!

2365
01:27:29,312 --> 01:27:30,613
Lame.

2366
01:27:30,647 --> 01:27:33,148
... or how he was separated
from his capsule.

2367
01:27:33,182 --> 01:27:36,918
Then who
or what has landed here?

2368
01:27:36,953 --> 01:27:38,320
I thought we covered that.

2369
01:27:38,353 --> 01:27:42,125
Is it here yet, or has
the cosmic switch been pulled?

2370
01:27:42,158 --> 01:27:43,225
You make the call!

2371
01:27:43,258 --> 01:27:45,060
Case in point:

2372
01:27:45,093 --> 01:27:47,497
The line between
science fiction

2373
01:27:47,530 --> 01:27:50,433
- and science fact...
- And science crap.

2374
01:27:50,467 --> 01:27:52,568
... is microscopically thin.

2375
01:27:52,602 --> 01:27:56,472
You have witnessed the line
being shaved even thinner.

2376
01:27:56,505 --> 01:27:58,942
- Mm-hmm.
- Golly, the joke's on us.

2377
01:27:58,975 --> 01:28:00,777
- But is the menace with us?
- Boo!

2378
01:28:00,810 --> 01:28:02,512
- Or is the monster gone?
- Ohh.

2379
01:28:02,545 --> 01:28:04,080
Boo!

2380
01:28:04,113 --> 01:28:05,382
- Whoa!
- Boo!

2381
01:28:05,415 --> 01:28:06,482
- Boo!
- Terrible.

2382
01:28:06,515 --> 01:28:08,017
[Overlapping chatter]

2383
01:28:08,050 --> 01:28:10,152
Oh, I've got an idea
to cheer us up.

2384
01:28:10,185 --> 01:28:12,855
[Whooshing and creaking]

2385
01:28:18,828 --> 01:28:22,832
Okay, I knew this movie might
get you down, Tom, so voila!

2386
01:28:22,865 --> 01:28:24,567
You're a happy king!

2387
01:28:24,600 --> 01:28:26,602
♪♪ [Imitating fanfare]

2388
01:28:26,635 --> 01:28:29,105
Great little song there, Joel,
real dignified.

2389
01:28:29,138 --> 01:28:30,873
Think I'll go
throw myself out an airlock.

2390
01:28:30,907 --> 01:28:32,475
Oh, come back here, Tom,
come on.

2391
01:28:32,508 --> 01:28:34,043
Every-- you know,
every kid on earth

2392
01:28:34,077 --> 01:28:36,445
dreams of becoming
a happy king.

2393
01:28:36,478 --> 01:28:38,113
♪♪ [Imitating trumpet fanfare]

2394
01:28:38,147 --> 01:28:39,648
Yeah, fine,
Joel, whatever.

2395
01:28:39,682 --> 01:28:41,250
I just rolled off
the turnip truck.

2396
01:28:41,283 --> 01:28:42,852
And, crow t. Robot,

2397
01:28:42,885 --> 01:28:46,422
by the power vested in me
by the kingdom of cookieville,

2398
01:28:46,455 --> 01:28:49,825
I now pronounce you
sir giggles Von laughs-a-lot.

2399
01:28:49,858 --> 01:28:53,763
Joel, I beg you not pronounce me
sir giggles Von laughs-a-lot.

2400
01:28:53,797 --> 01:28:56,898
Your job, sir giggles,
is to make sure that king Tom

2401
01:28:56,932 --> 01:28:59,235
remains a happy
and cheerful king.

2402
01:28:59,268 --> 01:29:01,737
♪♪ [Imitating trumpet fanfare]

2403
01:29:01,770 --> 01:29:03,538
- [Sobbing]
- Hey, what--

2404
01:29:03,572 --> 01:29:05,307
what's wrong?

2405
01:29:05,340 --> 01:29:07,177
Joel, it's this movie.

2406
01:29:07,210 --> 01:29:08,610
It was really
depressing.

2407
01:29:08,643 --> 01:29:10,813
It was like--
it was like being a little kid

2408
01:29:10,847 --> 01:29:13,348
and eating dinner at your aunt
Ruth's apartment in the suburbs,

2409
01:29:13,382 --> 01:29:14,683
and it's hot in there,

2410
01:29:14,717 --> 01:29:16,518
and she's got a local
Christian radio station on,

2411
01:29:16,552 --> 01:29:18,120
and there's nothing to do
or look at

2412
01:29:18,153 --> 01:29:19,988
'cause all she's
got in the apartment

2413
01:29:20,022 --> 01:29:22,692
are "good housekeeping"
magazines and linen doilies.

2414
01:29:22,725 --> 01:29:24,127
Yeah, and then
they send you out

2415
01:29:24,160 --> 01:29:26,228
to play with the strange
neighbor kids,

2416
01:29:26,262 --> 01:29:28,330
and they're all big,
and their skin is pink,

2417
01:29:28,363 --> 01:29:31,733
and they have big pores,
and the big eighth-grader

2418
01:29:31,767 --> 01:29:34,403
makes you look
at really upsetting pictures.

2419
01:29:34,437 --> 01:29:35,938
And so you go back inside
and sit down,

2420
01:29:35,972 --> 01:29:37,173
and they're
all just talking,

2421
01:29:37,207 --> 01:29:39,608
and there are big pauses
in their conversation.

2422
01:29:39,642 --> 01:29:42,545
And you can hear the clock
ticking on the wall!

2423
01:29:42,578 --> 01:29:44,313
Yeah, yeah, and so you
dig into your seat cushion,

2424
01:29:44,347 --> 01:29:47,015
and you find
a really old peanut,

2425
01:29:47,048 --> 01:29:48,752
and you're so bored,
you eat it.

2426
01:29:48,785 --> 01:29:51,420
And then you just feel bad
and a little sick and--

2427
01:29:51,453 --> 01:29:53,422
and then you think
you're about to go, but then--

2428
01:29:53,455 --> 01:29:55,390
then aunt Ruth
takes out a photo album

2429
01:29:55,425 --> 01:29:57,793
filled with black and white
photos of kids with squinty eyes

2430
01:29:57,827 --> 01:30:00,128
and they're supposed to be your
uncle and aunts or something.

2431
01:30:00,162 --> 01:30:02,165
And then your parents force you
to look at them!

2432
01:30:02,198 --> 01:30:03,800
Okay, okay,
come on, come on.

2433
01:30:03,833 --> 01:30:06,135
We're tougher than that,
you guys, come on.

2434
01:30:06,168 --> 01:30:07,937
Let's think of
something good about the movie.

2435
01:30:07,970 --> 01:30:10,005
Come on, sir mix-a-lot.

2436
01:30:10,038 --> 01:30:12,275
It's sir giggles
Von laughs-a-lot.

2437
01:30:12,308 --> 01:30:14,177
I mean, sir giggles Von
laughs-a-lot.

2438
01:30:14,210 --> 01:30:15,845
Um... oh...

2439
01:30:15,878 --> 01:30:17,913
- Come on.
- Uh... what?

2440
01:30:17,947 --> 01:30:20,917
Uh, oh, you couldn't hear
the dialogue.

2441
01:30:20,950 --> 01:30:22,585
Oh, right,
now that's a good one.

2442
01:30:22,618 --> 01:30:24,053
What about you,
king Tom?

2443
01:30:24,087 --> 01:30:25,455
Uh, okay, okay,
don't tell me.

2444
01:30:25,488 --> 01:30:27,857
No one involved
with this dung heap went--

2445
01:30:27,890 --> 01:30:29,392
never went on
to do anything else!

2446
01:30:29,425 --> 01:30:31,060
Right, all right,
that's a good thing.

2447
01:30:31,093 --> 01:30:33,328
You see, sirs, you can
throw us any crummy movie

2448
01:30:33,362 --> 01:30:34,897
you've got--
we can take it.

2449
01:30:34,930 --> 01:30:36,932
Or my name's not
Joel Robinson.

2450
01:30:36,965 --> 01:30:39,835
Yeah, my name's not Tom
"happy king" Servo!

2451
01:30:39,868 --> 01:30:41,337
Yeah, and my name
is not...

2452
01:30:41,370 --> 01:30:44,873
Crow t. Sir giggles
Von laughs-a-robot-whatever.

2453
01:30:44,907 --> 01:30:46,542
Yeah, and i'm
not even gypsy!

2454
01:30:46,575 --> 01:30:47,777
[All]
Yeah!

2455
01:30:47,810 --> 01:30:49,245
What do you think, sirs?
Yeah.

2456
01:30:49,278 --> 01:30:50,647
- [Blows raspberry]
- Ha!

2457
01:30:50,680 --> 01:30:51,713
Yeah.

2458
01:30:51,747 --> 01:30:53,148
That's fine, Joel.

2459
01:30:53,182 --> 01:30:54,650
Have your petty little
insurrection.

2460
01:30:54,683 --> 01:30:56,218
Just remember,
you're trapped in space,

2461
01:30:56,252 --> 01:30:58,053
dressed like happy kings,

2462
01:30:58,087 --> 01:30:59,688
and frank and I
are down here on earth,

2463
01:30:59,722 --> 01:31:01,490
free to do whatever we want.

2464
01:31:01,523 --> 01:31:04,060
Hey, Dr. F., there's a "Matlock"
marathon on tonight.

2465
01:31:04,093 --> 01:31:05,360
- You in?
- Oh!

2466
01:31:05,393 --> 01:31:07,128
Push the button, frank.

